{"assets":["/statement-assets/7d540bbc16f5d7702f83399681000828b59752bb7098e270b86d0ea993f5283f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2229","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I. The Endians"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a tree of $$$n$$$ nodes, where node $$$i$$$ has weight $$$w_i$$$, and an integer $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let the tree be rooted at node $$$x$$$. You may select a subset $$$S$$$ of the nodes such that $$$|S| = k$$$ and $$$x \\in S$$$. Let $$$f(i)$$$ be the sum of the weights of all nodes in $$$S$$$ on the path from node $$$i$$$ to the root. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"score"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$S$$$ is $$$\\sum_{i \\in S} f(i)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each node $$$1 \\le x \\le n$$$, find the maximum possible score among all subsets $$$S$$$ if the tree is rooted at node $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 500$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 4000$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$w_1, w_2,\\ldots, w_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le w_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n - 1$$$ lines contains two integers $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ ($$$1 \\le u, v \\le n$$$), indicating that nodes $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ are connected by an edge. It is guaranteed that the given graph is a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$4000$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print $$$n$$$ integers. For each $$$x$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, print the maximum possible score among all subsets $$$S$$$ if the tree is rooted at node $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n6 3\n2 12 3 6 9 7\n1 2\n1 3\n3 4\n4 5\n4 6\n5 5\n10000 1000 100 10 1\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n3 5\n9 5\n7 11 5 16 13 10 12 9 15\n8 1\n1 6\n3 7\n4 6\n6 7\n6 5\n9 1\n2 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n27 57 30 39 51 45 \n54311 15311 12511 12451 12415 \n120 150 134 170 155 122 150 132 162 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the tree is as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/7d540bbc16f5d7702f83399681000828b59752bb7098e270b86d0ea993f5283f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each $$$1 \\le x \\le n$$$, the following is an optimal set $$$S$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 1$$$: $$$S = \\{1, 2, 5\\}$$$; the score is $$$(2) + (12 + 2) + (9 + 2) = 27$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 2$$$: $$$S = \\{2, 4 ,5\\}$$$; the score is $$$(12) + (6 + 12) + (9 + 6 + 12) = 57$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 3$$$: $$$S = \\{2, 3, 5\\}$$$; the score is $$$(12 + 3) + (3) + (9 + 3) = 30$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 4$$$: $$$S = \\{2, 4, 5\\}$$$; the score is $$$(12 + 6) + (6) + (9 + 6) = 39$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 5$$$: $$$S = \\{2, 4 ,5\\}$$$; the score is $$$(12 + 6 + 9) + (6 + 9) + (9) = 51$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$x = 6$$$: $$$S = \\{2 ,4, 6\\}$$$; the score is $$$(12 + 6 + 7) + (6 + 7) + (7) = 45$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$S = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$$$ for all $$$x$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"I","problemCode":"2229I","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2229/problem/I"}